{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"moss\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Develop the smallest source-bound assessment and recovery precursor. Related capabilities have been searched. moss-source-bound-hazelnut-interior-access-trial already supplies inspection and process release, which must be reused rather than reinvented. opened-hazelnut-preparation-assessment supplies related assessment machinery but is bound to a different specimen and requires an owned unreserved assembly; source-bound-opened-hazelnut-access-trial likewise has different source bindings and only permits exterior rim contact. Neither establishes access to this actual completed, possibly still locked assembly. Add a paid assessment of current reachable access, locks and supported handling prerequisites, with an explicit route to existing release and pickup. Do not introduce an unsupported separation operation.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Development handoff: implement a source-bound exposed-assembly prerequisite assessment, recording code reuse from moss-source-bound-hazelnut-interior-access-trial for process identity, inspection boundaries, lifetime contact ledger and release; from opened-hazelnut-preparation-assessment for private evidence-limited reports; and from baseline pickup for local recovery. These are dependencies, not newly invented functions. Bind references to actor moss, specimen item-140-moss-811 from forest-hazelnut-1, stone item-171-moss-994, support start-2-stone, completed process manual-178-moss-1044 and optional complete personal record nut-opening:manual-178-moss-1044. Resolve actual live records at execution; the supplied fragments do not establish their current locations, reservations or full geometry. Never create replacement inputs or grant mastery.\\\\nModes: assess(processId, specimenId, toolId, supportId, evidenceRefs up to eight exact complete personal keys) and explicitly selected release(processId). Assess costs one active round and 0.5 energy, with zero material consumption, wear, displacement or reservations. Validate process/source lineage, lawful observational access, reach and sufficient energy before charging. Observation of an assembly held by this actor's original process is allowed only through that process's existing inspection authorization; a conflicting lock is reported, not bypassed. An owned inventory item is not required merely to assess the supported local assembly. Empty inventory is not evidence that the assembly or tool has vanished. Assess is atomic: no partial paid report or work accrues before commit. Absent targets, failed access or insufficient energy produce a bounded failure without an assessment charge; missing geometric support after a valid paid observation is reported as unresolved, not as successful physical access.\\\\nReport dated actual locations/access status, process status, reservation owner and release eligibility relevant to the actor's own process, reachable visible surfaces and supported external clearance. Do not expose unrelated private state or hidden material properties. Distinguish the tick-180 observation of discontinuity and limited pale compact surface from a new observation; neither establishes the whole interior, a kernel, edible material, an aperture large enough for handling, detachability or safety. Use the existing geometry resolution 0.02 and uncertainty 0.01 only where its response model supports observation; otherwise record unavailable geometry. Preserve exact source revisions and event/evidence citations. Report whether existing local pickup of the whole assembly and tool is supported after release; do not infer that support from proximity to the stone alone. A separation-readiness section identifies missing actual actuator, clearance, retention model, support or receiver only as applicable and unresolved, without fabricating prerequisites or issuing an executable separation quote. No impact, prying, internal insertion, sampling or trial is authorized by assessment.\\\\nRelease is a separately selected delegation to the existing cancel/release contract of moss-source-bound-hazelnut-interior-access-trial for manual-178-moss-1044, including a completed process when its locks remain. Add no material, energy or work charge to that existing administrative release and no physical pickup. Validate authority and live process state; atomically release only that process's remaining locks once at the actual assembly/tool locations. Repeated release is an idempotent no-op. If completed-state dispatch currently prevents the contractually promised release, repair that dispatch in the existing process handler rather than creating a second release ledger. Retain paid contacts, irreversible exposure, tool wear, provenance and ordinary ageing. Both opening contacts remain exhausted permanently; cancellation, recovery and learning never reset them. If locks are already clear, report that fact without moving anything. Existing local pickup must subsequently be chosen for each surviving item, independently validating reach, access and carrying limits and using its established time/energy terms. No remote return, restoration, duplicate item or free stock.\\\\nConservation: assembly quantity remains one retained source assembly, with all represented matter and internal bookkeeping retained; tool remains the same actual stone and support is not consumed. Assessment/release output only a private evidence report and observable process-state events, not shell/kernel fractions, food, debris, tool repair or new material. No separation in this release. A later explicitly requested conserved trial can enter development with its actual response model, force/work bound, inputs, output accounting and failure behavior; it is not rejected merely because a primitive is presently absent.\\\\nWork/lifecycle: study and assessment require actual actor time, with no progress during review/development waiting. Assessment has no ongoing process, escrow or maintenance. Interruption, cancellation or death before its atomic commit produces no report or assessment charge; completed effort and records are not refunded. Release is atomic and idempotent; death cleanup follows the original process's once-only local release contract. Original process progress survives interruptions and recovery, and no consumed effort is refunded. Existing ageing and other ordinary ongoing processes continue only when world time actually advances. Enforce these conditions in executable validation and lifecycle code, not repeated model review. No automatic physical work, communication, ingestion, healing, nutrition or benefit is supplied.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":1,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Moss studies individually for one active round costing 0.2 energy; no existing or new mastery is granted by this review. Study, requests, assessment registration, release and pickup earn no experience benefit by themselves. This precursor grants zero pleasure, maintained satisfaction, practice or comfort reward: repeated exposure and reports of missing mechanisms do not establish new information gain. Any future qualifying verified observation, including an informative physical failure, must use an existing applicable coded rule with personal relevance, canonical specimen/property/state deduplication, amount/cap, cooldown and decay; it must not create a reward account. No protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions change; nutrition is not mood-scaled and no physical-comfort increase is granted.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Reuse actual specimen, stone and support visuals without inventing anatomy or revealed contents. Emit assessment-completed, assessment-unresolved/blocked and process-release events only for the actions actually committed, citing actor, tick, source IDs/revisions, process ID, action status and report ID. Reusable visual metadata should include component=assessment-overlay, target references, state, evidence-event references, observed-region reference where actually supported, resolution/uncertainty and a label such as 'Limited exposure; separation unresolved'. Keep the detailed report personal. An overlay is UI metadata, not a material object. Display unlocked/released status only after verified release; display recovered/carried status only after successful baseline pickup. No opened-whole-interior, detached-food, safety, success sparkle or completed-trial imagery for incomplete, blocked or unsupported actions. No passive visual refresh or beneficial ongoing effect.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"9dd24f5a-ef10-4b9e-8cf3-ecb1cef0f193","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","observed"]},"search":{"type":"string","maxLength":400},"ids":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":240}},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"part":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}}}},"result_json":{"type":["string","null"]}}},"strict":true},"verbosity":"medium"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8240,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens_details":{"ttl_30m_tokens":0,"ttl_12h_tokens":0}},"output_tokens":1661,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":111},"total_tokens":9901,"attribution":{"items":{"msg_0